From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 05:10:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] s2r: publish the mailbox only for a verified reset
 vector (T8132)

The warm boot path assumes that every core resets into this image's
_vectors_start. That held by construction (stage 1 copies this stage over
its own base, and smp.c refuses to start a secondary otherwise), but
nothing checked it at the moment the mailbox is handed to the kernel.

Before publishing /chosen/asahi,s2r-mailbox, read every valid core's
RVBAR again (smp_verified_reset_vector()): all must be locked to this
image's _vectors_start. If not, publish no mailbox and log why. The kernel
then has no warm boot entry and keeps s2idle. If they match, also publish
/chosen/asahi,s2r-reset-vector with that address. The kernel can compare
it with the live boot core RVBAR before it arms the mailbox, so a kernel
never arms a warm boot through a vector this m1n1 did not verify.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/s2r.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 src/smp.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/smp.h |  1 +
 3 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/s2r.c b/src/s2r.c
index 036d0d63..f4244503 100644
--- a/src/s2r.c
+++ b/src/s2r.c
@@ -39,6 +39,8 @@
 #include "utils.h"
 #include "wdt.h"
 
+extern u8 _vectors_start[0];
+
 bool s2r_warm_quiet = false;
 
 /* Reset through the watchdog this m1n1 found at boot; spin if that fails */
@@ -129,13 +131,27 @@ int s2r_publish(void *dt)
     memset(&s2r_mailbox, 0, sizeof(s2r_mailbox));
     dc_civac_range(&s2r_mailbox, sizeof(s2r_mailbox));
 
+    /*
+     * The warm path exists only if every core resets into this image. Publish
+     * nothing otherwise: without the mailbox the kernel keeps s2idle.
+     */
+    u64 vector = smp_verified_reset_vector();
+    if (!vector) {
+        printf("FDT: RVBAR is not this image's vector %p on every core; no suspend-to-RAM mailbox\n",
+               _vectors_start);
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     int node = fdt_path_offset(dt, "/chosen");
     if (node < 0)
         return -1;
 
     if (fdt_setprop_u64(dt, node, "asahi,s2r-mailbox", (u64)&s2r_mailbox))
         return -1;
+    /* The kernel compares this with the live RVBAR before it arms the mailbox */
+    if (fdt_setprop_u64(dt, node, "asahi,s2r-reset-vector", vector))
+        return -1;
 
-    printf("FDT: suspend-to-RAM warm boot mailbox at %p\n", &s2r_mailbox);
+    printf("FDT: suspend-to-RAM warm boot mailbox at %p, reset vector 0x%lx\n", &s2r_mailbox, vector);
     return 0;
 }
diff --git a/src/smp.c b/src/smp.c
index b5dbf65b..96228486 100644
--- a/src/smp.c
+++ b/src/smp.c
@@ -994,6 +994,28 @@ uint64_t smp_get_mpidr(int cpu)
     return spin_table[cpu].mpidr;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The vector every core resets into, or 0. Only when each valid core's RVBAR is
+ * locked to the same address and that address is this image's _vectors_start:
+ * the precondition for a warm boot entry through this image (s2r.c).
+ */
+u64 smp_verified_reset_vector(void)
+{
+    if (!smp_initialized)
+        return 0;
+
+    u64 vector = 0;
+    for (int i = 0; i < MAX_CPUS; i++) {
+        if (!cpu_info[i].valid)
+            continue;
+        u64 rvbar = read64(cpu_info[i].impl_reg);
+        if (!(rvbar & RVBAR_LOCK) || (rvbar & RVBAR_ADDR) != (u64)_vectors_start)
+            return 0;
+        vector = rvbar & RVBAR_ADDR;
+    }
+    return vector;
+}
+
 u64 smp_get_release_addr(int cpu)
 {
     if (cpu < 0 || cpu >= MAX_CPUS)
diff --git a/src/smp.h b/src/smp.h
index df554374..a5566f2e 100644
--- a/src/smp.h
+++ b/src/smp.h
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@ bool smp_has_pending_calls(void);
 bool smp_is_alive(int cpu);
 uint64_t smp_get_mpidr(int cpu);
 u64 smp_get_release_addr(int cpu);
+u64 smp_verified_reset_vector(void);
 void smp_set_wfe_mode(bool new_mode);
 void smp_send_ipi(int cpu);
 
